items.docMarkdown:
Decodes a canonical Chia Bech32m address (`xch1...` or `txch1...`) into `(hrp, puzzle_hash)`.

Validates length bounds, enforces BIP-350 single-case formatting, splits on the last `'1'`
separator, verifies `"xch"` or `"txch"` network prefixes, checks the 6-character GF(2^5)
Bech32m checksum against [`BECH32M_CONST`], and unpacks the 52 5-bit payload words back into a
32-byte Chia puzzle hash—all using fixed stack buffers with zero heap allocations.

# Arguments

* `addr` - Candidate Chia Bech32m address string (either all-lowercase or all-uppercase ASCII).

# Returns

* `Some(("xch", puzzle_hash))` or `Some(("txch", puzzle_hash))` if `addr` is a valid 32-byte
  Chia mainnet or testnet address.
* `None` if `addr` fails length checks, mixes uppercase and lowercase, uses an unsupported HRP,
  contains invalid Bech32 characters, fails the checksum, or has invalid 5-to-8-bit padding.

# Complexity

`O(1)` time and `O(1)` stack memory (inputs outside `8..=100` bytes are rejected in constant time).

# Examples

```rust
use dbrain_core_rs::bech32m::{decode_chia_address, encode_chia_address};

let puzzle_hash = [0x42u8; 32];
let addr = encode_chia_address(&puzzle_hash, "xch");

let (hrp, decoded_hash) = decode_chia_address(&addr).expect("valid Chia address");
assert_eq!(hrp, "xch");
assert_eq!(decoded_hash, puzzle_hash);

// Mixed-case strings and corrupted checksums are strictly rejected:
assert!(decode_chia_address("Xch1invalid").is_none());
```

