items.docMarkdown:
Encodes a 32-byte Chia puzzle hash into a canonical lowercase Bech32m address (`xch1...` / `txch1...`).

Converts the 256-bit `puzzle_hash` into 52 five-bit words (zero-padding the final 4 bits),
computes the 6-symbol BIP-350 Bech32m checksum over the lowercased `hrp` and payload on stack
buffers, and formats the result into a single pre-sized `String`.

# Arguments

* `puzzle_hash` - 32-byte Chia puzzle hash to encode.
* `hrp` - Human-readable network prefix (typically `"xch"` for mainnet or `"txch"` for testnet;
  automatically normalized to ASCII lowercase).

# Returns

Canonical lowercase Bech32m address string (`<hrp>1<52-char-payload><6-char-checksum>`).

# Complexity

`O(1)` time for the fixed 32-byte puzzle hash (plus `O(hrp.len())` prefix handling), performing
a single exact-capacity output `String` allocation.

# Examples

```rust
use dbrain_core_rs::bech32m::{decode_chia_address, encode_chia_address};

let zero_puzzle_hash = [0u8; 32];
let testnet_addr = encode_chia_address(&zero_puzzle_hash, "TXCH");

// "txch" (4) + "1" (1) + 52 payload chars + 6 checksum chars = 63 characters
assert!(testnet_addr.starts_with("txch1"));
assert_eq!(testnet_addr.len(), 63);
assert_eq!(decode_chia_address(&testnet_addr), Some(("txch", zero_puzzle_hash)));
```

