items.docMarkdown:
Compresses a bijection `permutation[0..N]` into the canonical `BENES01\0` binary wire format.

Recursively decomposes `permutation` through Waksman/Beneš 2-colored input/output switch layers
until sub-permutations reach `leaf_size = 1 << middle_group_log2` (`<= 32`), then packs leaf
permutations as `u128` Lehmer factoradic bitfields behind the 22-byte `BENES01\0` header.

# Arguments

* `permutation` - Slice representing a bijection over `0..(permutation.len() as u32)`.
* `middle_group_log2` - Base-2 logarithm of the factoradic leaf block size (`0..=5`, corresponding
  to leaf sizes `1..=32`; e.g., `5` uses 32-element 118-bit factoradic leaves).

# Returns

Self-contained `BENES01\0` byte vector ready for on-disk storage, network transmission, or
direct `O(log N)` queries via [`route_benes_forward`] and [`route_benes_inverse`].

# Complexity

`O(N log N)` time and `O(N log N)` bits (`O(N)` bytes) in the returned compressed buffer.

# Examples

```rust
use dbrain_core_rs::benes::{
    compress_benes_permutation, route_benes_forward, route_benes_inverse,
};

let perm = [3u32, 0, 4, 1, 2]; // Odd N = 5 exercises odd-wire top pinning
let blob = compress_benes_permutation(&perm, 1); // leaf_size = 2^1 = 2

assert_eq!(&blob[0..8], b"BENES01\0");
for (x, &expected_y) in perm.iter().enumerate() {
    assert_eq!(route_benes_forward(&blob, x), expected_y);
    assert_eq!(route_benes_inverse(&blob, expected_y as usize), x as u32);
}
```

