Concatenates `delegated_puzzle_hash || vault_puzzle_hash` into a 64-byte signing payload.

Used by CHIP-0043 puzzle-scoped MIPS signers where an authorization applies to any coin sharing
`vault_puzzle_hash` rather than locking to a single coin ID.

# Arguments

* `delegated_puzzle_hash` - 32-byte tree hash of the inner delegated Chialisp puzzle being authorized.
* `vault_puzzle_hash` - 32-byte puzzle hash of the vault coin executing the delegated puzzle.

# Returns

Fixed 64-byte stack array `[delegated_puzzle_hash (0..32) || vault_puzzle_hash (32..64)]`.

# Complexity

`O(1)` time and `O(1)` stack space (two 32-byte `memcpy` operations, zero heap allocations).

# Examples

```rust
use dbrain_core_rs::clear_signing::calculate_vault_puzzle_message;

let delegated = [0xAAu8; 32];
let vault_ph = [0xBBu8; 32];
let msg = calculate_vault_puzzle_message(&delegated, &vault_ph);

assert_eq!(&msg[0..32], &delegated);
assert_eq!(&msg[32..64], &vault_ph);
```

