items.docMarkdown:
Concatenates `delegated_puzzle_hash || vault_coin_id || genesis_challenge` into a 96-byte signing payload.

Provides maximum replay protection for CHIP-0043 vault spends: binding `vault_coin_id` prevents
replaying the signature on future vault coins (since Chia coin IDs are unique and single-use),
while binding `genesis_challenge` prevents cross-network replay between testnet and mainnet.

# Arguments

* `delegated_puzzle_hash` - 32-byte tree hash of the (possibly wrapped) delegated puzzle.
* `vault_coin_id` - 32-byte unique Chia coin ID of the vault singleton coin being spent.
* `genesis_challenge` - 32-byte network genesis challenge (`AGG_SIG_ME` domain constant).

# Returns

Fixed 96-byte stack array `[delegated_puzzle_hash || vault_coin_id || genesis_challenge]`.

# Complexity

`O(1)` time and `O(1)` stack space (three 32-byte `memcpy` operations, zero heap allocations).

# Examples

```rust
use dbrain_core_rs::clear_signing::calculate_vault_coin_message;

let delegated = [0x01u8; 32];
let coin_id = [0x02u8; 32];
let genesis = [0x03u8; 32];
let msg = calculate_vault_coin_message(&delegated, &coin_id, &genesis);

assert_eq!(&msg[0..32], &delegated);
assert_eq!(&msg[32..64], &coin_id);
assert_eq!(&msg[64..96], &genesis);
```

