Calculates the wrapped delegated puzzle hash signed by an air-gapped recovery key during vault recovery.

Mirrors `chia_sdk_driver::clear_signing::vault_recovery_delegated_puzzle_hash`: constructs the
`Force1of2RestrictedVariable` timelock commitment, stacks the five opcode/coin-creation
restriction guards (`60`, `62`, `66`, `67`, `prevent_multiple_create_coins`), optionally
appends `force_singleton_recreation` when `version == VaultVersion::ForceSingletonRecreation`,
and folds all 6 or 7 wrappers from innermost to outermost around `delegated_puzzle_hash`.

# Arguments

* `delegated_puzzle_hash` - 32-byte tree hash of the inner recovery action puzzle.
* `left_side_subtree_hash` - 32-byte MIPS custody left-branch commitment curried into `Force1of2`.
* `recovery_timelock` - Required recovery delay in seconds (encoded as 8-byte big-endian `u64`).
* `version` - [`VaultVersion::Legacy`] (6 wrappers) or [`VaultVersion::ForceSingletonRecreation`] (7 wrappers).

# Returns

The 32-byte outer curried recovery delegated puzzle hash.

# Complexity

`O(1)` time (13 or 15 SHA-256 evaluations depending on `version`) and bounded memory.

# Examples

```rust
use dbrain_core_rs::clear_signing::{vault_recovery_delegated_puzzle_hash, VaultVersion};

let inner = [0x11u8; 32];
let subtree = [0x22u8; 32];

let v1 = vault_recovery_delegated_puzzle_hash(&inner, &subtree, 86_400, VaultVersion::Legacy);
let v2 = vault_recovery_delegated_puzzle_hash(
    &inner,
    &subtree,
    86_400,
    VaultVersion::ForceSingletonRecreation,
);

// Adding the 7th innermost ForceSingletonRecreation gate produces a distinct puzzle hash:
assert_ne!(v1, v2);
```

