items.docMarkdown:
Computes the 96-byte replay-protected message signed by a recovery key to initiate vault recovery.

Wraps `delegated_puzzle_hash` inside the 6- or 7-layer CHIP-0043 MIPS recovery restriction stack
via [`vault_recovery_delegated_puzzle_hash`] and binds the resulting outer puzzle hash to
`vault_coin_id` and `genesis_challenge` via [`calculate_vault_coin_message`].

# Arguments

* `delegated_puzzle_hash` - 32-byte tree hash of the inner recovery action puzzle.
* `left_side_subtree_hash` - 32-byte MIPS custody left-branch commitment.
* `recovery_timelock` - Required recovery delay in seconds.
* `vault_coin_id` - 32-byte coin ID of the vault singleton coin entering recovery.
* `genesis_challenge` - 32-byte Chia network genesis challenge (mainnet or testnet).
* `version` - [`VaultVersion`] selecting 6-gate legacy or 7-gate singleton-preserving recovery.

# Returns

Fixed 96-byte signing payload `[wrapped_recovery_hash || vault_coin_id || genesis_challenge]`.

# Complexity

`O(1)` time and bounded memory.

# Examples

```rust
use dbrain_core_rs::clear_signing::{
    calculate_vault_start_recovery_message, vault_recovery_delegated_puzzle_hash, VaultVersion,
};

let inner = [0x01u8; 32];
let subtree = [0x02u8; 32];
let coin_id = [0x03u8; 32];
let genesis = [0x04u8; 32];

let msg = calculate_vault_start_recovery_message(
    &inner,
    &subtree,
    3600,
    &coin_id,
    &genesis,
    VaultVersion::ForceSingletonRecreation,
);
let expected_prefix = vault_recovery_delegated_puzzle_hash(
    &inner,
    &subtree,
    3600,
    VaultVersion::ForceSingletonRecreation,
);

assert_eq!(&msg[0..32], &expected_prefix);
assert_eq!(&msg[32..64], &coin_id);
assert_eq!(&msg[64..96], &genesis);
```

