items.docMarkdown:
Computes the 32-byte FIPS 180-4 SHA-256 digest of `data` with zero heap allocations.

Streams `data` in 64-byte chunks through the standalone SHA-256 compression function, applies
standard Merkle-Damgård `0x80` bit padding and 64-bit big-endian bit-length framing in a
128-byte stack buffer, and serializes the 8 state words to a 32-byte big-endian digest.

# Arguments

* `data` - Arbitrary input byte slice to hash.

# Returns

The 32-byte (`256-bit`) SHA-256 cryptographic digest.

# Complexity

`O(N)` time where `N = data.len()` (`ceil((N + 9) / 64)` compression blocks) and `O(1)` stack
space.

# Examples

```rust
use dbrain_core_rs::merkle::sha256_digest;

// NIST FIPS 180-4 test vector for the empty string "":
// e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855
let empty_hash = sha256_digest(b"");
assert_eq!(&empty_hash[0..4], &[0xe3, 0xb0, 0xc4, 0x42]);
assert_eq!(&empty_hash[28..32], &[0x78, 0x52, 0xb8, 0x55]);

// NIST test vector for "abc": ba7816bf...
let abc_hash = sha256_digest(b"abc");
assert_eq!(&abc_hash[0..4], &[0xba, 0x78, 0x16, 0xbf]);
```

