Computes `SHA-256(0x01 || left32 || right32)` per the DIG Network D5 interior node specification.

Prepends the `0x01` interior-node domain separation tag before concatenating `left32` and
`right32` on a 65-byte stack array, ensuring interior Merkle branch digests can never collide
with leaf digests (preventing Merkle tree second-preimage attacks). Also serves as the
binary tree-hash combiner when currying Chialisp delegated puzzle wrappers in
[`crate::clear_signing::wrap_delegated_puzzle_hash`].

# Arguments

* `left32` - 32-byte digest of the left child node.
* `right32` - 32-byte digest of the right child node.

# Returns

The 32-byte domain-separated SHA-256 interior parent digest.

# Complexity

`O(1)` time (two SHA-256 block compressions over a 65-byte stack preimage) and `O(1)` stack space.

# Examples

```rust
use dbrain_core_rs::merkle::{dig_hash_pair, sha256_digest};

let left = [0x11u8; 32];
let right = [0x22u8; 32];
let parent = dig_hash_pair(&left, &right);

// Left/right child ordering is cryptographically bound (non-commutative):
assert_ne!(parent, dig_hash_pair(&right, &left));

// Matches explicit `0x01 || left || right` preimage hashing:
let mut preimage = [0u8; 65];
preimage[0] = 0x01;
preimage[1..33].copy_from_slice(&left);
preimage[33..65].copy_from_slice(&right);
assert_eq!(parent, sha256_digest(&preimage));
```

