items.docMarkdown:
Builds a 16-band sorted Multi-Probe LSH index over `signatures`.

Extracts 16 ten-bit band keys per signature via [`extract_lsh_bands_16x16`] and sorts each
band table unstably by `band_key` so bucket ranges occupy contiguous cache lines for fast
`partition_point` binary searches.

# Arguments

* `signatures` - Slice of `N` 1,024-bit (`[u64; 16]`) capsule embeddings (`N <= u32::MAX`).

# Returns

Ready-to-query [`MultiProbeLshIndex1024`] instance.

# Complexity

`O(N log N)` construction time (16 sorts of `N` 64-bit `(u16, u32)` tuples) and `O(N)` memory.

# Examples

```rust
use dbrain_core_rs::recall::{compute_bq_embedding_1024, MultiProbeLshIndex1024};

let s0 = compute_bq_embedding_1024("alpha beta gamma");
let s1 = compute_bq_embedding_1024("delta epsilon zeta");
let index = MultiProbeLshIndex1024::build(&[s0, s1]);

let (hits, _) = index.query_multi_probe(&s1, false, 1);
assert_eq!(hits[0].0, 1);
```

