items.docMarkdown:
Queries the index with `0-bit` exact band keys and optional `1-bit` neighbor multi-probes.

For each of the 16 bands, probes `base_key` (`p = 0`) and—when `enable_one_bit_probes` is
`true`—each of the 10 single-bit-flipped keys `base_key ^ (1 << (p - 1))` (`p = 1..=10`).
Deduplicates hit `doc_id`s with a boolean `seen` bitmap, re-scores only those unique
candidates via [`bq_hamming_similarity_1024`], and returns the top `top_k` matches sorted
descending by similarity alongside the total number of unique candidates evaluated.

# Arguments

* `query_sig` - 1,024-bit (`[u64; 16]`) query signature from [`compute_bq_embedding_1024`].
* `enable_one_bit_probes` - When `true`, probes 10 single-bit Hamming neighbors per band
  (`176` total bucket lookups) in addition to exact band matches (`16` lookups).
* `top_k` - Maximum number of highest-similarity `(doc_id, similarity)` pairs to return.

# Returns

Tuple `(results, evaluated_count)` where `results` contains up to `top_k` `(doc_id, similarity)`
pairs ordered from highest to lowest similarity, and `evaluated_count` is the total number
of unique candidate documents re-ranked.

# Complexity

`O(16 * P * log N + C log C)` time where `P` is `11` (`enable_one_bit_probes == true`) or `1`
(`false`), and `C <= N` is the number of unique bucket candidates (`evaluated_count`).

# Examples

```rust
use dbrain_core_rs::recall::{compute_bq_embedding_1024, MultiProbeLshIndex1024};

let doc_crypto = compute_bq_embedding_1024("chia bls12_381 signature aggregation");
let doc_merkle = compute_bq_embedding_1024("dig network merkle inclusion tree arena");
let index = MultiProbeLshIndex1024::build(&[doc_crypto, doc_merkle]);

let query = compute_bq_embedding_1024("dig network merkle inclusion proof arena");
let (top_hits, evaluated) = index.query_multi_probe(&query, true, 1);

assert_eq!(top_hits[0].0, 1);
assert!(top_hits[0].1 > 0.70);
assert!(evaluated >= 1);
```

